# Project overview

**Name:** Japan Evangelistic Band (repo: `japan-evangelistic-band`)

**What it is:** PWA idle/management game — American missionary life in Tokyo. iPhone-first via GitHub Pages (Add to Home Screen). Dark theme, sakura + gold palette; Japanese UI text unlocks as language skill grows.

**Deploy:** GitHub → Settings → Pages → branch `claude/environment-selection-iphone-EohwW` → `/` (root)

**Live URL:** https://spellmynameright.github.io/japan-evangelistic-band/

**Stack:** Pure HTML, CSS, vanilla JS — no build step, no framework, no `package.json`. ES modules, `localStorage` saves (`tokyo_called_v1`), Web Audio API, PWA (`manifest.json` + `sw.js`).

**Key files:** `index.html`, `css/style.css`, `js/main.js` (boot/hooks), `js/state.js` (single source of truth), `js/engine.js` (1s tick), `js/ui.js` (render), plus `actions`, `locations`, `npcs`, `milestones`, `language`, `resources`, `save`, `audio`.

**Architecture (short):** All modules mutate `state` from `state.js`. Engine ticks every 1s; `main.js` wires hooks; `requestAnimationFrame` drives `renderFrame()` in `ui.js`.

Full file map, state shape, tables, and UI IDs are in `CLAUDE.md`.
